### L2. Second escape list and single-quoted literals (OPEN-6, item 16)
* **Pick:** **(a)**
* **Runner-up:** (b)
* **Cited:** 2026-11-08 items 16, 33 (OPEN-6), 49 (OPEN-18); `decisions.md` OD137, Core Q4.2; `PHILOSOPHY.md` rule 2 (one form) & rule 3 (transparency).
* **Reason (52 words):** Item 16 explicitly states "quoted ASCII literals, patterns, comparisons migrate explicitly" to `u8`, and item 33 keeps "exactly two escape lists". Retaining `'a'` as an ASCII `u8` literal with `\'` preserves both items verbatim, adheres to OD137 (ASCII-only), and cleanly disambiguates `'a'` from `'label` by closing-quote lookahead.
* **Missing option:** Unified 7-escape list (`\n \t \r \0 \\ \" \'`) shared across both string and ASCII byte literals (revising item 33 to one list while keeping `'a'` literals).

### L3. Raw control characters in string literals (OPEN-6)
* **Pick:** **(a)**
* **Runner-up:** (b)
* **Cited:** 2026-11-08 item 30 (OPEN-1), item 33 (OPEN-6); `decisions.md` Core Q4.1–Q4.4; `PHILOSOPHY.md` rule 3 (transparency) & rule 4 (verbosity never argues against clarity).
* **Reason (44 words):** OPEN-6 explicitly recommends "no raw line breaks/control characters". Refusing raw tabs and control bytes (0x00–0x1F, 0x7F) inside string literals ensures every non-printable byte is visibly written as `\t`, `\0`, etc., preventing invisible source-text ambiguity between spaces, tabs, and control codes during audit.
* **Missing option:** None.

### L4. Integer suffix grammar and base prefixes (OPEN-5)
* **Pick:** **(a)**
* **Runner-up:** (b)
* **Cited:** 2026-11-08 items 41 (OPEN-5), 59; `decisions.md` slice-0 surface (leading-zero refusal), Q6.2 (`200u8`), OD31, OD63, OD138; `PHILOSOPHY.md` rule 2 (one form).
* **Reason (51 words):** OPEN-5 recommends lowercase base prefixes (`0x`/`0b`/`0o`), no `_` separators, no float suffixes, and retaining typed integer suffixes (`i8`..`u64`) directly adjacent to digits. Allowing suffixes across all four bases (`0xffu8`) avoids arbitrary base-specific exceptions while keeping one canonical spelling per base and width.
* **Missing option:** Require expected-type inference everywhere and drop suffixes by rewriting Q6.2's example (already rejected by item 41).

