### S1-move. Source text for reading a linear (non-Copy) value
* **Pick:** **(a)**
* **Runner-up:** (b)
* **Cited:** `decisions.md` Q9.1 (read forms), OD62; `PHILOSOPHY.md` rule 2 (one form), rule 3 (transparency), rule 4 (verbosity), rule 9 (linear ownership), conflict priority 2 & 4 (transparency & explicitness beat brevity).
* **Reason (53 words):** In Concrete, most code is written by models and audited by humans (`PHILOSOPHY.md`). Writing `move t` in source makes ownership transfer and use-site consumption immediately visible without looking up `t`'s declaration to check `Copy`, matching Core Q9.1 directly and satisfying conflict priorities 2 (transparency) and 4 (explicitness).
